rl":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-11-29T07:02:26Z","updated_at":"2019-11-29T07:18:52Z","body":"crashing in `win_set_minimal_style` . Doing some debugging, I see that `win_valid(wp)` is false just after  the ` win_enter(wp,...)` call in `nvim_open_win`.\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.093 8437  win_new_float:576: xxx new win: 0x1684a60\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.094 8437  win_new_float:576: xxx new win: 0x1688870\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.095 8437  nvim_open_win:1102: xxx after win_enter: 0x1688870\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.098 8437  win_new_float:576: xxx new win: 0x1694dd0\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.099 8437  win_close:2433: xxx closing win: 0x1694dd0\r\nERROR 2019-11-28T22:59:42.099 8437  nvim_open_win:1102: xxx after win_enter: 0x1694dd0\r\n```\r\n\r\n `win_enter(...,trigger_enter_autocmds=true)` triggers the `CursorMoved` event which closes the just-created window, which is then invalid further in the codepath.\r\n\r\nClosing a window as soon as it's created isn't really what you wanted, the script should specify `<buffer>`:\r\n\r\n    api.nvim_command(\"autocmd CursorMoved <buffer> ++once \"..floating_win..\"wincmd c\")\r\n\r\nBut of course the bug should be fixed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/559682361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"htt